 backstory: `
House Viridane's archivist. He was the one who realized, five years after the flight, that the seven families were not merely altering records, they were systematically hunting down and destroying every document that contained the Viridane name. Rather than let the families' arcanists take the archive, Torven burned it himself. Forty years of genealogies, treaty records, correspondence, and legal precedents, all of it, committed to fire in a single night in a moonlit grove, while the fae watched in silence.

He spent the remaining thirty years of his life transcribing what he could remember into the oral tradition, reciting lineages to anyone who would listen, training the first generation of Trueborn memory-keepers in the art of the spoken archive. His thorns, according to the oral history he himself helped establish, migrated over his lifetime from his hands, where he held the pen, to his tongue, where he held the words. By the time he died, he could barely speak around the thorn-cluster, but every word that emerged was a preserved fragment of Viridane's history. The Trueborn consider him the father of their tradition. the Shorn rarely speak his name, his burning of the archive is, to them, a reminder of everything they have chosen to hide rather than preserve.
 `
