 name: 'Aurel Shorn-First',
 title: 'The One Who Chose to Pass',
 portraitIcon: 'Elves/Icon11',
 backstory: `
The first Shorn. Three generations after the flight, when the Briaran had established themselves in the groves and the erasure was complete, Aurel looked at the world outside the mist and made a calculation: the seven families would never stop hunting. The groves would never be safe. The only way to ensure the bloodline's survival was to stop being visible. She shaved her thorns flat to the skin, took a human name, Mara Fellwood, and walked into a Frostwood Reach port town alone.

Within a year she had established a trade business. Within five she had married a human merchant who never suspected. Within twenty she had three children who did not know what they were. She told them on her deathbed, pressing a piece of ghost-metal into each of their hands, and then died under a name that was not hers, mourned by a community that had never known her. the Shorn consider her the practical savior of the bloodline. The Trueborn consider her the first to do the seven families' work for them. Both are correct.
 `
